+# A Codex implementation dispatch declares a model and effort but passes and observes neither
+
+## Description
+
+The model routing of a project names, per duty and runner, the model and effort an implementation dispatch should run on (the greenfield project declared `gpt-6-luna` at effort `high` for the Codex implementer). The Codex prepare command prints the arguments of the `spawn_agent` call as `{ agent_type, message }` only, so no model or effort reaches the tool layer, and nothing observes what the child ran on. The dispatch record of such a run says so itself: `modelAssurance: declared-unobserved`, "model and effort are the briefing's declaration, not an observation". In the run, the six implementation children reported `gpt-6.1-sol` while the briefings and the record named `gpt-6-luna`; the readiness reviewer ran on `gpt-6-luna` and the two Critics on `gpt-6-sol`. The difference is evidenced; whether it cost quality or money is not, and the cause (the role's own configuration, an inherited session model, or an ignored prompt line) is not provable from the report.
+
+## Triggering situation
+
+The Codex greenfield report of the candidate 31 run (priority P0.2 of that report). `policies/model-policy.md` MP-29 already states that a model named only in the dispatch text does not steer the tool layer.
+
+## Affected artifact
+
+`plugins/pipeline-core/scripts/codex-native-dispatch-prepare.mjs` (the printed `spawn_agent` arguments), the SubagentStart/SubagentStop hooks of `native-goldfish-host.mjs` (what they could observe), the dispatch record (`modelAssurance`), the projected Codex role files, `policies/model-policy.md` MP-29.
+
+## Proposal
+
+1. Probe once, live, which arguments the Codex `spawn_agent` tool accepts and which model and effort the SubagentStart payload reports; nothing should be built before that is measured.
+2. If the tool takes a model and effort, let the prepare command print them from the routing and let the guard compare the call with the routing before the first product write.
+3. If the hook reports the child's model, record it in the dispatch record as an observation and show a typed mismatch beside the declaration (a notice, as on Antigravity, never silently).
+4. If neither exists, say so in the dispatch record and the briefing instead of naming a model as if it were set.
+
